<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">
	<PropertyGroup>
		<TargetFrameworks>netstandard2.0;net462;net8.0</TargetFrameworks>
		<LangVersion>latest</LangVersion>
		<ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>
		<Nullable>enable</Nullable>
		<IsPackable>true</IsPackable>
		<!-- The analyzers of trimming and NativeAOT run on the target that has them. -->
		<IsAotCompatible Condition="$([MSBuild]::IsTargetFrameworkCompatible('$(TargetFramework)', 'net8.0'))">true</IsAotCompatible>
		<VersionPrefix>2.9.1</VersionPrefix>
		<PackageId>ChromaDB.Client</PackageId>
		<!-- -p:PackageIdPrefix=Name publishes the package as Name.Client. -->
		<PackageId Condition="'$(PackageIdPrefix)' != ''">$(PackageIdPrefix).Client</PackageId>
		<Authors>ssone95, cincuranet, ChromaDotNet contributors</Authors>
		<PackageDescription>.NET client for Chroma and Chroma Cloud, tested with Chroma 0.4.10 to 1.5.9. Community project, not affiliated with Chroma.</PackageDescription>
		<PackageTags>chroma chromadb vector-database chroma-cloud ai embeddings rag</PackageTags>
		<PackageReadmeFile>README.md</PackageReadmeFile>
		<!-- The logo of ChromaDotNet goes only in the packages published with -p:PackageIdPrefix. -->
		<PackageIcon Condition="'$(PackageIdPrefix)' != ''">icon.png</PackageIcon>
		<PackageLicenseExpression>MIT</PackageLicenseExpression>
		<RepositoryType>git</RepositoryType>
		<RepositoryUrl>https://github.com/ssone95/ChromaDB.Client</RepositoryUrl>
		<PackageProjectUrl>https://github.com/ssone95/ChromaDB.Client</PackageProjectUrl>
		<!-- In GitHub Actions the links point to the repository that builds the package. -->
		<RepositoryUrl Condition="'$(GITHUB_REPOSITORY)' != ''">https://github.com/$(GITHUB_REPOSITORY)</RepositoryUrl>
		<PackageProjectUrl Condition="'$(GITHUB_REPOSITORY)' != ''">https://github.com/$(GITHUB_REPOSITORY)</PackageProjectUrl>
		<IncludeSymbols>true</IncludeSymbols>
		<!-- The XML documentation of the public API goes in the package, for IntelliSense. -->
		<GenerateDocumentationFile>true</GenerateDocumentationFile>
		<NoWarn>$(NoWarn);RS0026;RS0027</NoWarn>
		<SymbolPackageFormat>snupkg</SymbolPackageFormat>
		<PackageReleaseNotes>2.9.1: the buckets of db.client.operation.duration are the boundaries of the OpenTelemetry semantic conventions, 0.001 to 10 s, which OpenTelemetry 1.10 and later apply (the net8.0 build takes System.Diagnostics.DiagnosticSource 9.0.20; on the netstandard2.0 build the application adds a view); a chain of filters with the same operator goes as one list, so 32 filters and more no longer throw, and the client splits long lists so that a single Chroma server neither rejects nor crashes on them; AddAsync throws an ArgumentException for a null metadata value, which deletes the key in UpdateAsync and UpsertAsync; the known defects of the Chroma servers in docs/COMPATIBILITY.md. 2.9.0: the settings of a new collection: the HNSW index (ChromaHnswConfiguration), the SPANN index of Chroma Cloud (ChromaSpannConfiguration) and the embedding function it declares; the indexes of the values in a schema, WithIndex and WithoutIndex; on Chroma Cloud, MaxScore sparse indexes and a customer-managed key, WithGcpCmek; the embedding function in ModifyConfigurationAsync; ChromaCollection.Dimension, Version and LogPosition; doubles and floats written with the fewest digits that read back as them, whole ones as floats, and read right on .NET Framework; the integer HNSW settings of the metadata, like hnsw:construction_ef, as integers; an ArgumentException before the request for what a server would store changed or drop: lone surrogates, ulongs above long.MaxValue, empty lists in the metadata of records, lists in the metadata of collections, names that the path of a URL drops, an HNSW index with fewer than 2 neighbors; the netstandard2.0 build takes the 8.0 packages, with no warnings on .NET 6 and 7; the package icon and the vector-database tag. 2.8.0: the BM25 vectors computed from the schema and text queries in SparseKnn, as the Python client of Chroma does; the space of a collection with a schema; writes in batches and reads in pages by default, 300 records at a time on Chroma Cloud, and the quota a rejection tells; traces and metrics with OpenTelemetry (ChromaTelemetry); ChromaConfigurationOptions.FromConnectionString; clients that tests can mock; ids in QueryAsync; ChromaEmbeddingFunctionReference.Known, for the other functions of a schema; a .NET Framework 4.6.2 build, which runs next to OpenTelemetry without binding redirects; every parameter and result documented. The API follows the .NET conventions, the Async suffix and read-only lists among them: how to adapt in $(PackageProjectUrl)/releases/tag/v2.8.0. 2.7.1: the description of the package says that it is a community project, not affiliated with Chroma, and the tags have chroma-cloud. 2.7.0: for Chroma Cloud, the Search API: ChromaCollectionClient.Search with ChromaSearch, ChromaRank (Knn, SparseKnn, Rrf and the arithmetic of ranks) and ChromaSearchGroupBy; sparse vectors in metadata, ChromaSparseVector, and the schema of a collection with sparse vector indexes, ChromaCollectionSchema and ChromaCollection.SparseVectorIndexes; ChromaBm25, the BM25 function of Chroma, with the same vectors as its Python client; Add, Update and Upsert compute the BM25 vectors that the schema declares, and SparseKnn takes a text, as the Python client does; new ChromaClient(uri) and new ChromaClient(options), with an HttpClient of their own that Dispose closes. 2.6.0: the rest of the v2 API: ChromaWhereDocumentOperator.Regex and NotRegex; Delete(ChromaDelete) by filters, with a limit and the count of the deleted records; ModifyConfiguration, for the settings of the index of the collection; Healthcheck; Count(ChromaReadLevel); ChromaClient.WithTenantAndDatabaseFromIdentity; for Chroma Cloud Fork, ForkCount, GetIndexingStatus, AttachFunction, GetAttachedFunction, DetachFunction, GetCollectionByCrn and UpdateTenant. XML documentation in the package. Fixed: ChromaCollection.Space also reads the space that Chroma Cloud sends in the spann configuration; the validation errors of the 0.x servers are the message of the exception. 2.5.0: embeddings in base64 where the server declares supports_base64_encoding; WithBatchSplitting(maxBatchSize) for servers like Chroma Cloud, which declares 1000 but takes 300 records per write; ChromaException.ErrorType; CollectionExists also by a NotFoundError about a collection. 2.4.1: works in applications published with trimming or NativeAOT: serialization with metadata generated at build time, IsAotCompatible. All the releases: $(PackageProjectUrl)/releases. Tested versions: $(PackageProjectUrl)/blob/main/docs/COMPATIBILITY.md. Migration from 1.x: $(PackageProjectUrl)#migrating-from-chromadbclient-1x</PackageReleaseNotes>
	</PropertyGroup>
	<ItemGroup>
		<!-- The public API, checked at build: PublicAPI.Shipped.txt is the API of the last release, PublicAPI.Unshipped.txt what was
		     added since. RS0026 and RS0027 are about overloads with optional parameters, the design the API already has. -->
		<PackageReference Include="Microsoft.CodeAnalysis.PublicApiAnalyzers" Version="5.6.0" PrivateAssets="all" />
	</ItemGroup>
	<ItemGroup>
		<None Include="..\README.md" Pack="true" PackagePath="\" />
		<None Include="..\assets\chromadotnet-icon.png" Pack="true" PackagePath="\icon.png" Condition="'$(PackageIdPrefix)' != ''" />
		<None Include="..\LICENSE" Pack="true" PackagePath="\" />
		<None Include="..\THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md" Pack="true" PackagePath="\" />
	</ItemGroup>
	<ItemGroup Condition="'$(TargetFramework)'=='netstandard2.0' Or '$(TargetFramework)'=='net462'">
		<PackageReference Include="PolySharp" Version="1.14.1">
			<PrivateAssets>all</PrivateAssets>
			<IncludeAssets>runtime; build; native; contentfiles; analyzers</IncludeAssets>
		</PackageReference>
	</ItemGroup>
	<!-- The netstandard2.0 build is the one of .NET Core 3.1 to 7: the 8.0 packages have builds for .NET 6 and 7, and no
	     warning there, as 2.7.1. ActivitySource and Meter are in the runtime from .NET 5. -->
	<ItemGroup Condition="'$(TargetFramework)'=='netstandard2.0'">
		<PackageReference Include="System.Memory" Version="4.5.5" />
		<PackageReference Include="System.Diagnostics.DiagnosticSource" Version="8.0.1" />
		<PackageReference Include="System.Text.Json" Version="8.0.6" />
	</ItemGroup>
	<!-- .NET 8: InstrumentAdvice, for the bucket boundaries of db.client.operation.duration, is in DiagnosticSource 9 and later,
	     which OpenTelemetry 1.10 and later bring too. -->
	<ItemGroup Condition="'$(TargetFramework)'=='net8.0'">
		<PackageReference Include="System.Diagnostics.DiagnosticSource" Version="9.0.20" />
	</ItemGroup>
	<!-- .NET Framework: the versions OpenTelemetry 1.19 brings, so that the two load without binding redirects. -->
	<ItemGroup Condition="'$(TargetFramework)'=='net462'">
		<PackageReference Include="System.Memory" Version="4.6.3" />
		<PackageReference Include="System.Diagnostics.DiagnosticSource" Version="10.0.12" />
		<PackageReference Include="System.Text.Json" Version="10.0.12" />
		<Reference Include="System.Net.Http" />
		<!-- The implicit usings of .NET Framework do not have it. -->
		<Using Include="System.Net.Http" />
	</ItemGroup>
</Project>
